Final Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (991–1000)
991. Improper Validation of API Request Methods
HTTP Method Authorization Bypass
Applications fail to restrict certain HTTP methods (PUT, DELETE, PATCH), allowing attackers to perform unauthorized actions.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
992. Insecure Handling of Password Reset Tokens
Password Reset Token Reuse
Reset tokens remain valid after use, enabling attackers to reuse them.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
993. Improper Validation of API Data Exports
API Data Export Exposure
Export APIs leak sensitive user or system data.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
994. Insecure Handling of Shared Workspace APIs
Workspace Authorization Bypass
Attackers gain access to shared workspaces belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
995. Improper Validation of Login Session Management
Session Fixation
Attackers reuse or control user sessions before authentication.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
996. Insecure Handling of Cloud Configuration Files
Cloud Configuration Exposure
Configuration files reveal API keys or access credentials.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
997. Improper Validation of User Permission APIs
Permission Escalation Vulnerability
Attackers elevate privileges to access restricted functions.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
998. Insecure Handling of API Debug Parameters
Debug Parameter Information Disclosure
Debug parameters expose backend system details.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
999. Improper Validation of Data Synchronization Permissions
Data Sync Authorization Bypass
Attackers synchronize or retrieve data belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
1000. Insecure Handling of System Backup Files
Backup File Exposure
Backup files accessible online expose databases, credentials, or private information.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
